#===============================================================================
# MINIMAL VISIBILITY TEST — Sharket 3.29 Ruthless
#
# QUESTION: Ruthless forbids `Hide`. We emit `Minimal`, which still draws a
# label. Can style lines make a Minimal block effectively INVISIBLE?
#
# HOW TO RUN
#   1. Select this filter instead of your normal one.
#   2. Play anywhere that drops common currency (any zone, a few minutes).
#   3. Each variant below is bound to ONE very common base and has its OWN
#      SOUND. When you hear a sound, look at the ground and note whether you
#      can see a label, and how loud it is.
#   4. Everything not listed keeps a normal label, so the game stays playable.
#
# WHAT EACH SOUND MEANS
#   sound 1  A control      — Minimal, no style. This is what V7.0 ships now.
#   sound 2  B fontsize 1   — does the game clamp it, or honour it?
#   sound 3  C transparent  — text + plate + border all at alpha 0
#   sound 4  D Sharket full — fontsize 1 AND all three transparent
#   sound 6  E fontsize 18  — the documented minimum, for comparison
#   sound 7  F Show + full  — the 3.15 form, on a Show block instead of Minimal
#
# WHAT WE ARE TRYING TO LEARN
#   * Does `Minimal` honour style lines at all? (A vs B/C/D)
#   * Is `SetFontSize 1` clamped up to 18? (B vs E — if B and E look the
#     SAME, it clamped; if B is smaller, it did not.)
#   * Is alpha 0 enough on its own? (C)
#   * Does `Show` behave differently from `Minimal` for the same style? (D vs F)
#
# ⚠️ F is a `Show` block on purpose. If F is invisible but D is not, then the
#    quiet layer should be built from styled Shows, not from Minimal — which
#    would be a real change to how this filter hides things.
#
# ⚠️ Our generator currently STRIPS every style line from a hide block
#    (filterStyle.blockText), so none of B–E can be produced by the generator
#    today. This file is hand-written for the test. If a variant wins, that
#    strip rule is what has to change.
#===============================================================================


#--- A · CONTROL — Minimal with no style (exactly what V7.0 emits) -------------
Minimal
    BaseType == "Scroll of Wisdom"
    PlayAlertSound 1 300


#--- B · Minimal + SetFontSize 1 ----------------------------------------------
Minimal
    BaseType == "Portal Scroll"
    SetFontSize 1
    PlayAlertSound 2 300


#--- C · Minimal + fully transparent text / plate / border --------------------
Minimal
    BaseType == "Armourer's Scrap"
    SetTextColor 0 0 0 0
    SetBackgroundColor 0 0 0 0
    SetBorderColor 0 0 0 0
    PlayAlertSound 3 300


#--- D · Minimal + the full Sharket 3.15 recipe -------------------------------
#     fontsize 1 AND all three channels transparent
Minimal
    BaseType == "Blacksmith's Whetstone"
    SetFontSize 1
    SetTextColor 0 0 0 0
    SetBackgroundColor 0 0 0 0
    SetBorderColor 0 0 0 0
    PlayAlertSound 4 300


#--- E · Minimal + SetFontSize 18 (documented minimum) ------------------------
#     If B looks identical to E, the game clamped 1 up to 18.
Minimal
    BaseType == "Orb of Transmutation"
    SetFontSize 18
    PlayAlertSound 6 300


#--- F · SHOW + the full recipe (the actual 3.15 form) ------------------------
#     A Show block certainly honours style. If this is invisible and D is not,
#     the quiet layer belongs on Show, not Minimal.
Show
    BaseType == "Orb of Augmentation"
    SetFontSize 1
    SetTextColor 0 0 0 0
    SetBackgroundColor 0 0 0 0
    SetBorderColor 0 0 0 0
    PlayAlertSound 7 300


#--- reference · a normal loud label, so you can calibrate --------------------
Show
    BaseType == "Orb of Alteration"
    SetFontSize 45
    SetTextColor 0 0 0 255
    SetBackgroundColor 255 207 132 255
    SetBorderColor 255 255 255 255
    PlayAlertSound 10 300
    MinimapIcon 1 Yellow Diamond


#--- everything else keeps a normal label so the game stays playable ----------
Show
